            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of sepsis in perspective: what have 25 years of sepsis definition brought us?]</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1841</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first official definition of sepsis was published in 1992. Last year, in 2016, the third version was published. In this article we discuss the various definitions, the evolving insights into pathophysiology and several of the treatments that have been implemented over the last 25 years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
